{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.MagicLadderEquivalences","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.MagicLadderEquivalences","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality","lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MagicLadderEquivalences.primality_iff_condensation_for_n_ge_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MagicLadderEquivalences.primality_iff_condensation_for_n_ge_2","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MagicLadderEquivalences.lean#L56-L79","doc":"**Theorem.** For `n ≥ 2`, algebraic primality at `q_0`\n(conjecture A) is equivalent to homological shell condensation\n(conjecture C). The `n = 1` case is excluded because A's\n`empiricalMagicLadder` contains 1 (vacuously) while C's\n`magicLadder` does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.MagicLadderEquivalences.predicate_equivalence_via_magic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.MagicLadderEquivalences.predicate_equivalence_via_magic","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/MagicLadderEquivalences.lean#L39-L52","doc":"**Meta-theorem (transitivity through the magic ladder).** Given\ntwo predicates `P, Q : ℕ → Prop` that each satisfy the iff\n`P n ↔ n ∈ magicLadder` and `Q n ↔ n ∈ magicLadder`, they are\npairwise equivalent: `P n ↔ Q n` for every `n`.\n\nProof: chain the two iffs through the middle term. ","signatureChunk":0}]}